NO WEB APP SUBSTITUTION

Do not solve any AMAN requirement by creating a web interface and placing it inside a WebView.

Do not use WebView as the application's primary UI.

Do not create an HTML-based imitation of the Android application.

Supabase is the backend/data platform; it does not change the fact that the client product is a native Android application.

The architecture must therefore be:

Android UI
    ↓
ViewModel / Presentation
    ↓
Repository / Data Layer
    ↓
Supabase Client
    ↓
Supabase Auth / PostgreSQL / RPC / RLS

and not:

Android WebView
    ↓
Website
    ↓
Web Backend

